LLM generates it, by FILLING SCHEMAS the game already loads: the sandbox
map JSON and the persona/look/trait record formats. The model never
places anything; a validator gates the one load path, its errors go back
to the model verbatim (cap 3), and results open as editable drafts. One
atomic commit per issue.

**#125 validation layer** (`a4c9881`) — validateCast wraps the EXISTING
loaders and adds generation needs: nearest-valid-id suggestions (edit
distance over the catalog), inline valid-trait lists, batch name
uniqueness; extractJsonObject pulls balanced JSON out of fences/prose;
renderRetryFeedback formats errors for the next attempt. All offline —
every scaffold stub across all four of tonight's milestones is now a
live test.

**#126 cast generation + CLI** (`6038380`) — prompt builders with
closed-world vocabulary blocks; `worldgen_cli` drives the full headless
loop (gen-cast / gen-map / gen-village / validate-*) and emits a
machine-readable stats line the bench keys on.

**#128 the measured iteration** (`b3277d5`) — the milestone's real
story: ALL THREE local models failed the first contract identically →
the contract was at fault (persona text inside JSON strings); switching
to one JSON object per character fixed it everywhere at once. Then
"style-consistent" kept failing → the vocabulary never said which
